[38;5;231m⏺[39m Added a checkbox to [38;5;153mindex.html:20-23[39m.

  - Native [38;5;153m<input type="checkbox">[39m wrapped in a [38;5;153m<label>[39m, so the on/off state is the browser's own and clicking the text
    toggles it too.
  - A CSS [38;5;153m:checked[39m rule strikes through the label text so "done" is visible. No JavaScript needed.

  One sample item is hardcoded as a placeholder. If items should come from a list (array, JSON, server), say the word
  and I'll wire it up — that's the piece the request left open.

  Not run/verified in a browser; it's static HTML with no test setup in the repo.

